From e23e41aca18ebf3df2393b6320e0d1b7153bf423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muxsinjon <Muxsinjon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:47:21 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Milestone 5: terrain-aware sunlight and Earth line of sight

- Verified existing planner horizon masks, terrain/geometric models,
  partial-disc handling, combined timelines and AVGVISIB overlays
- Time-dependent sunlight and Earth line-of-sight layers on the 3D terrain
  sites: 20 m mesh near field + LOLA 240 m far field (21x21x720 grids),
  upper-limb rule, 80 m evaluation, faded 1 km edge band
- NASA PGDA product 90 permanently shadowed regions (20 m) as static context
- Full / partial / disc-weighted sunlight metrics (terrain model only)
- Validation: native 5 m reference horizons (inner median 0.01-0.04 deg,
  p95 0.28-0.67 deg); PGDA AVGVISIB long-term agreement (median 0.9-2.0 pp);
  Shackleton PSR never lit; hourly vs 10-minute bound (<= 0.01 pp)
- Tests: terrainShadow/sunlight unit tests, test_illumination_sites.py,
  lighting e2e; smoke row count updated for the new rows
- Docs: MILESTONE5_ACCEPTANCE.md, PROJECT_STATUS, DATA_SOURCES, VALIDATION,
  AI_USAGE, README, CLAUDE.md, About disclaimers

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
